 { This position is taken from the game Čmilytė,V - Jonkman,H (2005). From here, White used tactics to create an outpost by force. Can you find the two-move sequence that she played? } 20. { -KEY- } f4 $1 { A clever pawn break! } Nd7 { Supporting the centre, but now White can play her idea. } ( { But not } 20... exf4 $2 { since after } 21. e5 $18 { White wins a piece. } ) 
21. f5 $1 { Correct! White now has a powerful central outpost on e6. } h6 { In the game, Black tried to resolve the tension straight away and invited the knight to take up its position on the outpost. } 22. Ne6 { The knight lands on the outpost, and already Black's position is close to indefensible. } Rf6 23. Rac1 { Shifting the focus to the c-file, while Black is busy fighting against the knight invasion. } Nf8 { Black tackles the knight, but it has cost him too much time. } 24. Nxd6 $1 cxd6 25. Rc7 $1 { Entry along the 7th rank proves decisive since Black has no good reply against the double threat. } Rf7 $2 { A blunder, but the position was already lost. } ( 25... Nxe6 { was the lesser evil, but after } 26. Rxe7 Nf8 27. Rxa7 $18 { White's connected passed pawns on the queenside are decisive. } ) 
26. Nxf8 { Simplifying the position. } ( 26. Nxg7 $1 { This tactical shot was even stronger, since after } Qxg7 ( 26. Nxf8 Rxg7 27. f6 { is also hopeless. } ) 
27. Rxe7 $1 Rxe7 28. f6 Qf7 29. fxe7 Qxe7 30. Bxh6 $18 { White is up material, and will be able to crash through against the naked Black king. } ) 
Qxf8 27. Rxa7 $18 { White's queenside pawns eventually decided the game in her favor. This game is an instructive example of how to combine various pawn play elements (pawn breaks, pawn advances) with tactics in order to secure an outpost. While Black was able to eliminate the knight, he could not at the same time control against an invasion on the queenside. This brings us to the end of this section on creating & maneuvering. If an outpost is already on the board, most of the time your goal will simply be to occupy it. In the case that there is no outpost, it pays to check if one can be created by changing the pawn structure. Since outposts are so valuable, players spend a lot of energy fighting for and against them. This is the topic of the next section. } 
 *
